1 type 0b00
ADD SUB AND OR XOR MV ADDI SHL SHR ROL ROR          add, neg, xor, shift, left, cyclic
funct1: 1st bit - sum or bitwise or\and
        2nd bit - 2nd operand - negative/(if sum = 0 => or|and)
        3d  bit - addi (if 1st bit is 1), xor (if first bit is 0)
funct2: 1st bit - need shift or not
        2nd bit - shift left\right
        3d  bit - cyclic shift
here s1 - first register, s2 - second register, rd - destination register, imm only used in addi
2 type 0b01
LW SW LI SB PUSH POP                                lower\upper
funct: 1st bit - read\write
       2nd bit - (if read - load immediate)(if write - write byte)
       3d  bit - (increment\decrement stack) (if this bit is one, than looking on 1st bit and defining push or pop)
hilo - if load immediate defines lower (upper - upper 12 signed bits)(lower - lower 20 bits)
d - add displacement from immediate
register is address (if LW or SW or SB) or pushing value, or register, where pop will be placed
if its LI register is a destination register
3 type 0b10
BEQZ BEQN BNEZ BNEN JMP LJMP                        comp, n/z, not
funct: 1st bit - (JMP or branch instruction) (if 1 => JMP)
       2/3 bit - (00 - BEQZ, 01 - BEQN, 10 - BNEZ, 11 - BNEN) if first bit is zero - defines JMP or long JMP(LJMP)
register is comparing value, immediate is a displacement
if its a jump, immediate value is displacement
if its long jump, register is an address

spec 0b11
INT IRET HALT CALL RET
register is a register with address
funct: 1st bit - is interruption
       2nd bit - is return (is interruption is zero, this bit defines call\ret, else int\iret)
       3d  bit - halt

